--
N5008 [temp.inst]/2-3: renamedt<ssa_exprt, L0> is named (by-value return type of
a declaration) while ssa_exprt is still incomplete, so its first elaboration
drops the base; once ssa_exprt is complete, the friend declaration inside
renamedt<exprt, L2> re-elaborates it NESTED in that instantiation.  The
re-elaboration arrived with empty specialization arguments, build() skipped
the arity mismatch and the body was substituted with the enclosing
instantiation's `underlyingt` = exprt, so get() returned const exprt& (the
goto-symex renaming_level.cpp "symbol 'identifier' is unknown").  For a
primary template the full arguments are the specialization arguments.
